#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186075045 :tutorial/content "To divide a unit fraction by a whole number, we multiply the fraction's denominator by the whole number.\n\nFor example, to calculate $\\dfrac{1}{5} \\div {\\color{blue}2},$ we multiply the fraction's denominator by ${\\color{blue}2}\\!:$\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{5} \\div {\\color{blue}2}  = \\dfrac{1}{5 \\times {\\color{blue}2}} = \\dfrac{1}{10}\n$$\n\nNotice that we get the same answer using a fraction model, and the process is similar.\n\n![](images/3f/3f1f0dddd115c0d820de4d79624bd87492e215a6c2de43071fda73a4a0684d77.png)" :tutorial/id #uuid "fcf4ea8b-7765-55e8-b5c1-a10899bee9f6" :tutorial/math-academy-id 8562 :tutorial/title "Introduction"}]}
